{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# DC sub-task parent sync: two live cells have never passed — they are WRONG ORACLES, plus one real silent-drop defect\n\nFiled under epic [rebar:e369-a449-4773-48fb]. Operator ruling (2026-08-04): **resolve the failures;\ndo NOT delete, skip, or `xfail` any cell.**\n\n## Evidence — never passed, measured across 12 consecutive harness runs\n\nPer-cell failing sets from every `Live External Integration` job `30834117797` (08-03 16:52) through\n`30951453979` (08-04 21:14). Both cells appear in the FAILED set of **all 12**:\n\n    test_inbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips     12/12 FAILED\n    test_outbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips    12/12 FAILED\n\n**\"Never passed\", NOT a regression** — no bisect, no revert. The harness demonstrably detects fixes\n(6 -> 3 failures over the window, with six named cells dropping out at identifiable runs); these two\nnever did.\n\n## Mechanism — RE-MEASURED, with two premises of the original filing corrected\n\n### Platform half — CONFIRMED (ticket 1a9f)\n\nDC 8.17.1 accepts `PUT fields.parent` on a sub-task and **silently ignores it**. Re-confirmed live in\nrun `30951453979`, whose own failure text is the measurement: rebar asked for `RBJREXN-2`, Jira\naccepted, a fresh REST read still reported `RBJREXN-1`. Capability map req-0056 (HTTP 204) /\nreq-0058 (read-back unchanged) hold. Re-asserting mattered because this epic RETRACTED the map's\nlabel-ceiling entry when a live cell contradicted it.\n\nClearing is separately impossible on a sub-task: `{\"fields\":{\"parent\":null}}` -> 400,\n`{\"update\":{\"parent\":[{\"set\":null}]}}` -> 400, sub-task `editmeta` exposes NO `parent` field\n(req-0054/0055/0057, [rebar:37e7-d751-0042-4b94]).\n\n### CORRECTION 1 — the apply-side symbol was mis-located, and the \"disjoint gates\" premise is REFUTED\n\n`set_parent` lives in **`adapters/jira_datacenter/_hierarchy.py:100`**, not `transport.py` (which\ncontains no parent code). And it no longer \"accepts only a sub-task child\": since 39c1/change 1311\nits non-sub-task branch WRITES the discovered Epic Link field (`_hierarchy.py:147-168`). The emit and\napply gates therefore **already overlap** for the epic shape, pinned on both sides — unit\n`test_dc_epic_link_parent_39c1.py:296` and live\n`test_outbound_epic_parent_reaches_dc_THROUGH_A_RECONCILE_PASS`, **PASSED in run 30951453979**. A\nreconcile pass demonstrably emits and lands a parent on DC today.\n\n### CORRECTION 2 — the remaining rebar defect is SILENCE, not disjointness\n\n`_resolve_local_parent` (`outbound_field_diff.py:138-139`) returns `(False, None)` for a non-epic\nparent — **byte-identical to :142's \"unbound this pass, retry next pass\"** — with no log call of any\nkind, and the caller at :383-385 does nothing when `not present`. So a user's parent edit against a\nnon-epic parent never enters `fields`, `dispatch_one._update_one_apply_parent:523` never runs, and\nthe entire `record_parent_divergence` / `bridge_alerts` apparatus (`pass_io.py:103-146`) is\n**structurally unreachable**. The pass exits 0 and reports convergence while the hierarchy diverges.\n\nThis violates the project's own contract, cited: `pass_io.py:113-118` — \"a log line is not a signal:\nthe pass still exits 0 and **nothing durable says the hierarchy diverged**\" — and\n`dispatch_one.py:561-564` — \"Warn-and-continue alone is why 'the parent never reached the tracker'\nstayed invisible through **five instances of this class**.\" 39c1 wired that contract into\n*apply-time* failure and left *emit-time* suppression silent. `record_parent_divergence` has **zero**\nreferences in `tests/`. This is an **incomplete implementation of 39c1 AC4** and is pure rebar,\nfixable with no platform capability.\n\n## THE RE-HOME TARGET, NAMED AND CAPABILITY-CHECKED\n\nAC1's answer is **negative for a genuine sub-task** and **positive for the Epic Link**, and the\nsupported mechanism is therefore named rather than assumed:\n\n> **The Epic Link custom field on a NON-sub-task child.** Both directions and both operations are\n> already GREEN on the live instance in run `30951453979`:\n> `test_outbound_epic_parent_round_trips_via_the_epic_link` (set AND clear, raw-REST read-back),\n> `test_outbound_epic_parent_reaches_dc_THROUGH_A_RECONCILE_PASS` (through a real pass), and\n> `test_inbound_clear_parent_round_trips` (Epic Link clear observed inbound via 9bb9's\n> `get_parent_map` fallback). Capability map req-0040/0041.\n\nRe-homing changes the CHILD SHAPE from sub-task to standard issue. That is the point, not a loss:\nan oracle for an operation the platform cannot perform is a wrong oracle. The **subject of each cell\nis preserved** — see AC4/AC5 below — and the platform impossibility stays pinned by the two cells\nthat already assert it (`test_a_subtask_reparent_is_REFUSED_rather_than_silently_ignored`, and\n37e7's sub-task-clear pin at `test_dc_mutations.py:1810-1817`), so a future DC that starts allowing\nit is caught rather than silently forgotten.\n\n**Why this ticket's ruling supersedes 1a9f's disposition.** 1a9f left the two round-trip cells RED\nand carried the loudness in a separate refusal cell. That left two permanent reds in a suite whose\nvalue is that a red means something, and the epic's goal is DC support **without** standing failures.\nThe operator's 2026-08-04 ruling for this ticket is to resolve them, and re-homing is the\nalready-endorsed instrument for exactly this shape — used by 37e7 (Row 13 inbound), b9b8 (Row 14),\nand [rebar:4b9e-bcad-456a-4233]. This ticket adopts that framing explicitly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] **AC1 — LIVE measurement of whether ANY supported DC mechanism moves a sub-task's parent.**\n      ANSWERED, run `30951453979`: `fields.parent` on a sub-task is accept-and-ignore (req-0056/0058,\n      reproduced in the run's own failure text); nulling it is 400 both spellings (req-0055/0057);\n      sub-task `editmeta` exposes no `parent` (req-0054). **Negative for a sub-task.** The supported\n      mechanism is the **Epic Link on a non-sub-task child**, green in the same run (req-0040/0041).\n- [ ] **AC2 — the emit side stops failing SILENTLY.** A non-epic parent the tracker cannot represent\n      must produce a durable, operator-visible record (a `bridge_alerts` entry), not a bare `return`\n      indistinguishable from \"retry next pass\". 8b25's guard is **preserved** — the field stays\n      omitted, so rebar still never issues a write DC would ignore. Scoped to what rebar controls;\n      this does not claim the sub-task shape becomes emittable.\n- [ ] **AC3 — no write DC is measured to accept-and-ignore is ever issued, and the unsupported case\n      fails LOUDLY** (raise + bridge alert naming the reason and the supported alternative), never a\n      silent no-op reporting success.\n- [ ] **AC4 — `test_inbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips` PASSES, re-homed, subject preserved.**\n      Its subject is **rebar's inbound pass carrying a parent change into `.parent_id`**; the DC-side\n      reparent was only SETUP, and that setup is the impossible part (it fails at\n      `test_dc_mutations.py:1664`, before the subject is ever reached). Re-homed to an Epic Link\n      re-parent (child under epic A, moved DC-side to epic B), the oracle still asserts the\n      user-visible outcome end to end: **the child ends up under the intended parent locally.**\n- [ ] **AC5 — `test_outbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips` PASSES, re-homed, subject preserved.**\n      Re-homing it to \"epic parent outbound\" would duplicate two already-green cells and assert\n      nothing new. Its live subject becomes the claim currently unasserted anywhere: **when a user\n      sets a parent the tracker cannot represent for this child shape, rebar must tell the operator\n      rather than dropping it.** The oracle asserts the user-visible outcome for the unsupported\n      case — a bridge alert naming the reason and the supported alternative, AND the remote parent\n      unchanged. This is a **rebar** capability, not a platform one, so it is reachable; and it is\n      distinct from `test_a_subtask_reparent_is_REFUSED_rather_than_silently_ignored`, which asserts\n      the transport-level raise, not what a PASS surfaces.\n- [ ] **AC6 — no cell is deleted, skipped, or `xfail`ed to reach green** (operator ruling). The\n      sub-task platform impossibility remains pinned by the two cells named above.\n- [ ] **AC7** — `docs/jira-dc-capability-map.md` records the outcome with run id `30951453979`.\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 --dist worksteal -q\n    gh workflow run \"Live External Integration\" --ref main   # the only place these cells run"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785884725192083001,"uuid":"0e5fab4a-edf6-4120-8ef0-f94e6cf5866f"}